WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:05.330
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:02.500 --> 00:04.170
The Yumimimi Festival.

00:04.460 --> 00:09.500
It is a festival of the Takamimi Shrine,
where we pray for peace at sea.

00:05.330 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:05.330 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:05.340 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:05.340 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:05.340 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:05.340 --> 00:08.290
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

00:11.290 --> 00:16.210
The main attraction is the bow ritual,
held on a boat on the Sumida River.

00:17.710 --> 00:22.580
It predicts whether or not there will be a good haul at sea
that year, and is a very important ritual.

00:23.670 --> 00:27.790
The archer shoots three arrows
at a target held by the shrine's deity,

00:24.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>Good</b>

00:24.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>haul</b>

00:25.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>Fairly</b>

00:25.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>good</b>

00:26.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>Normal</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>Maybe</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>next</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.580
<b>year...</b>

00:28.210 --> 00:33.170
and they say the closer the arrow lands to the center,
the better the fishing haul will be.

00:34.330 --> 00:40.960
My grandfather, the head priest of the shrine, got injured,
and it was decided that I'd play the part of the archer.

02:12.130 --> 02:14.960
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

02:12.130 --> 02:16.790
<b>EPISODE 12</b>

02:12.130 --> 02:16.790
<b>THIS IS MY</b>

02:12.130 --> 02:16.790
<b>SHRINE DEITY</b>

02:37.670 --> 02:41.210
Just as I thought, there's no way I can be the archer.

02:41.420 --> 02:45.960
N-no, I have a favorable impression
of the good-natured way you miss.

02:46.130 --> 02:47.830
You're trembling like crazy, though.

02:48.130 --> 02:51.960
W-well, there are only 3 days
until the Yumimimi Festival...

02:52.210 --> 02:53.420
You were watching, right?

02:53.420 --> 02:55.960
I didn't even graze the target
for all 3 of those shots!

02:56.670 --> 03:01.000
Y-yeah... no matter how I try to adjust,
you're pretty bad at this.

03:01.290 --> 03:06.540
Yeah, I know! Why does it fly
every which way else but straight?!

03:06.750 --> 03:10.630
W-well, a straight shot is the hardest one to make.

03:11.040 --> 03:16.540
There was much less warring in the Edo days,
and archery had developed as a martial art, but...

03:16.920 --> 03:20.670
There's also something called long-range archery,
where you only shoot straight.

03:20.750 --> 03:28.630
<b>From here</b>

03:21.040 --> 03:25.750
They shot arrows about 120 meters from under the eaves
of the Sanjuusangendo Hall,

03:24.750 --> 03:28.630
<b>To here</b>

03:25.920 --> 03:28.540
and they competed over
the number of arrows they shot through.

03:28.790 --> 03:31.000
There's even a competition like that?!

03:31.000 --> 03:34.830
Just like I thought,
there's no way I can do this in such a short time!

03:34.960 --> 03:39.000
W-well, there's no need to think about it so seriously.

03:39.290 --> 03:42.210
L-look, it's even written on that target, you know?

03:42.580 --> 03:45.630
It has "Don't bother comparing" written on it.

03:46.000 --> 03:50.130
It means don't think of this as a competition or game,
and it isn't about whether you hit or miss it.

03:46.540 --> 03:49.380
<b>Don't bother comparing</b>

03:50.130 --> 03:52.290
Just don't worry about it.

03:52.790 --> 03:54.710
Just take it easy.

03:55.040 --> 03:58.000
But everyone is looking forward to the Oyumi ritual...

03:58.420 --> 04:01.540
What am I gonna do if I miss all the shots
and disappoint everyone?!

04:01.880 --> 04:07.000
I'm so sorry to all of the parishioners
who have been so good to me!

04:07.000 --> 04:09.500
G-get ahold of yourself, Koito!

04:09.500 --> 04:12.880
If you panic, then I can't panic!

04:12.880 --> 04:16.000
I've got it! You're good
at shooting arrows, too, right Elda?

04:16.000 --> 04:17.830
Will you give me an example to go by?

04:17.830 --> 04:23.250
H-hmm... I guess I'll give it a try,
though it's been so long.

04:37.880 --> 04:41.500
Wow! You're awesome, Elda! Total bullseye!

04:41.750 --> 04:44.000
Is there some kind of trick to it or something?!

04:44.000 --> 04:46.750
A trick, huh? Ah, I know.

04:46.960 --> 04:51.250
Listen carefully, and you'll hear something
like the voice of the wind very well.

04:51.250 --> 04:52.080
Huh?

04:52.210 --> 04:58.040
At the right time, the wind will say "Now's the time,"
about the target, and you let it fly right then.

04:54.380 --> 04:55.500
<b>Now's the time</b>

04:57.960 --> 04:59.040
<b>Now's the time</b>

04:58.210 --> 04:59.670
The rest will take care of itself.

05:00.460 --> 05:00.710
<b>Now's the time</b>

05:00.500 --> 05:04.080
That kinda sounds like a trick specific to elves!

05:04.670 --> 05:08.380
Sh-should I be the archer like I was long ago?

05:08.460 --> 05:12.380
No, you don't want to fall from the boat again...

05:13.630 --> 05:15.790
I'll practice a bit more.

05:17.830 --> 05:18.750
Okay.

05:22.790 --> 05:25.080
The arrow won't hit me if I'm over this way.

05:29.130 --> 05:34.130
Sorry, Elda! No matter what I do,
it always goes towards you!

05:34.130 --> 05:36.580
Y-yeah, don't worry about it.

05:36.960 --> 05:40.420
This is an actual headshot...

05:41.290 --> 05:44.250
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

05:42.290 --> 05:48.130
In the middle of all that...
the day of the Yumimimi Festival finally arrived.

05:44.250 --> 05:49.000
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

05:44.250 --> 05:49.000
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

05:44.250 --> 05:49.000
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

05:44.250 --> 05:49.000
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

05:50.960 --> 05:55.750
Huh? Where's Elda-sama? Won't she be on
the portable shrine until she gets on the boat?

05:56.210 --> 05:59.540
She went ahead by car with Grampa and Koyuzu.

05:59.920 --> 06:03.880
There were more people than expected,
and she got cold feet and threw a tantrum.

06:04.040 --> 06:06.210
She sure is devoted to being a shut-in.

06:06.420 --> 06:07.710
I'd expect nothing less.

06:07.710 --> 06:11.670
For real. She never changes, that shrine deity of ours.

06:13.750 --> 06:15.580
Uh...yeah.

06:17.130 --> 06:19.540
So, how're the preparations going?

06:22.290 --> 06:23.710
I am hopeless.

06:23.830 --> 06:25.580
Like, I can't help but laugh.

06:25.580 --> 06:27.500
Yeah, that's not a surprise.

06:28.040 --> 06:31.250
Well, if it's a doozy of a miss and you get a laugh out of it,
I'd call that a huge success.

06:31.630 --> 06:34.500
I'll be the first to laugh, so go for it!

06:34.750 --> 06:37.130
Right. Thanks, Koma-chan.

06:45.250 --> 06:47.290
Okay, I'm heading out.

06:57.080 --> 06:58.380
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

07:04.040 --> 07:07.580
Bow! Bow! I call upon you, bow!

07:08.000 --> 07:11.670
Bow! Bow! I call upon you, bow!

07:12.130 --> 07:16.170
Bow! Bow! I call upon you, bow!

07:16.540 --> 07:20.630
Bow! Bow! I call upon you, bow!

07:52.210 --> 07:54.580
Are you all set, Koito?

07:55.880 --> 07:59.250
What? You're so quiet I can't hear you!

07:59.750 --> 08:01.670
"The one with the quick wit, Koito"?!

08:01.790 --> 08:03.330
N-no, no.

08:03.750 --> 08:06.330
Are you all set, Koito?!

08:07.580 --> 08:09.580
"Quick-wit Koito"?

08:09.750 --> 08:14.000
No! Are you all set, Koito?

08:14.000 --> 08:18.330
You mean, I can run quick? That's 'cause I run track!

08:18.330 --> 08:22.380
No, no. What are you talking about, Koito?

08:19.920 --> 08:23.330
E-everyone can hear you, Sis!

08:22.380 --> 08:25.330
What?! I can't hear you!

08:31.040 --> 08:36.290
Sure is rocky... At this rate I might really miss all of them.

08:37.420 --> 08:40.960
Y-yeah, the boat is scary, just as I thought.

08:51.460 --> 08:57.080
K-Koito! I won't get mad
even if you land a headshot, so take it easy!

08:57.580 --> 08:59.880
Y-you probably can't hear me, though!

09:00.580 --> 09:05.210
Yeah! I heard you clearly this time! Okay, here I go!

09:10.330 --> 09:12.080
Now, off it flies!

09:14.290 --> 09:16.130
Now, let it fly!

09:17.670 --> 09:20.420
Rid us of evil, Arrow of Takamimi!

09:26.500 --> 09:27.920
She missed.

09:28.330 --> 09:29.250
Way off...

09:31.330 --> 09:32.420
Two more chances.

09:46.630 --> 09:49.330
Wh-why is it only her bloodlust that was elevated?!

09:49.630 --> 09:53.380
J-just to confirm, you're not aiming
for a headshot, are you?!

09:53.380 --> 09:56.750
I'm not even sure where it's going to go, you know!

09:57.460 --> 10:02.290
This is the last one. You've got this... You can do it, Koito!

10:03.330 --> 10:05.750
Good luck, Sis!

10:26.250 --> 10:27.790
I'm sorry, Elda.

10:28.210 --> 10:31.170
I can't hit the target after all.

10:32.040 --> 10:35.630
I'll at least aim not to hit you, and shoot this one far!

10:52.920 --> 10:55.580
Goodness... I suppose I have no choice.

11:10.500 --> 11:12.750
Whaaaat, Elda?!

11:12.920 --> 11:14.420
Elda-sama?!

11:20.500 --> 11:21.210
Elda!

11:24.290 --> 11:25.630
Elda!

11:37.330 --> 11:38.920
Dead center!

11:38.920 --> 11:40.380
Hooray!

11:48.000 --> 11:51.170
Jeez, Elda! Why'd you jump in there?!

11:51.830 --> 11:55.710
Th-the arrow hit the bullseye, and I fell, too...

11:56.250 --> 12:00.380
W-we might have a super prosperous
fishing haul this year, right?

12:05.880 --> 12:06.670
Yup!

12:08.000 --> 12:12.080
Oh, Elda and Koi-chan truly are a great team.

12:13.080 --> 12:15.250
Are you watching, Sayoko?

12:18.790 --> 12:22.460
Your third shot was in the
"Maybe next year" territory, huh...?

12:24.500 --> 12:29.080
That's how, thanks to Elda,
the Yumimimi Festival ended in a huge success.

12:29.750 --> 12:35.710
The super excited parishioners gave us
a huge food stall gourmet as an offering.

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Takoyaki</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Yakisoba</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Corn Dogs</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Ramune</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Takoyaki</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Yakisoba</b>

12:32.670 --> 12:36.920
<b>Ramune</b>

12:36.960 --> 12:41.710
Whoa! I'm so happy that everyone
seemed pleased with it!

12:41.830 --> 12:42.420
Yeah!

12:42.670 --> 12:46.420
All right, I'm gonna do my best
at the Oyumi ritual next year, too!

12:46.420 --> 12:47.080
Er...

12:47.500 --> 12:50.880
K-Kikujirou can do it next year, can't he?

13:02.670 --> 13:05.500
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

13:08.460 --> 13:09.080
<b>Table</b>

13:08.460 --> 13:09.080
<b>Pepper</b>

13:22.080 --> 13:25.080
O-okay, one more level...

13:25.710 --> 13:28.670
One more level and I've reached my personal best...

13:28.670 --> 13:32.210
Koganei-sama, Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama.

13:33.750 --> 13:36.130
You have a delivery from Amazin!

13:36.540 --> 13:37.630
Huh?! Eh, wait...

13:39.290 --> 13:41.540
Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama!

13:42.420 --> 13:44.130
You have a delivery!

13:45.790 --> 13:46.830
Maybe no one's home?

13:55.630 --> 13:58.580
Hm? The flourescent light is out.

14:00.170 --> 14:02.330
There must be another in the kitchen...

14:09.630 --> 14:10.960
I'm back, Elda.

14:11.540 --> 14:14.330
Huh? I wonder why the light is out.

14:14.540 --> 14:15.630
Uh, whoa!

14:18.960 --> 14:23.630
I-I want to purify myself...

14:24.920 --> 14:27.080
Can you please explain this from the beginning?

14:28.330 --> 14:32.540
The truth is that recently, I've had no luck...

14:32.830 --> 14:36.080
Unfortunately, the cap on the pepper came off
and it spilled all over,

14:36.330 --> 14:39.460
and unfortunately, I missed a delivery,

14:39.460 --> 14:42.130
and unfortunately, I bashed my pinky toe...

14:43.420 --> 14:45.420
All the bad things are piling up!

14:45.580 --> 14:51.210
B-but, this isn't funny! I might have been cursed!

14:51.210 --> 14:53.000
Who would curse you?

14:54.080 --> 14:55.960
M-maybe you?

14:58.170 --> 15:01.500
I-I mean, I'm so sloppy...

15:01.500 --> 15:03.790
If you can break it, shall I actually try to curse you?

15:05.500 --> 15:07.500
But about that sort of thing...

15:07.960 --> 15:12.250
Maybe it's just that bad things
leave an impression on you more easily.

15:12.500 --> 15:15.580
N-no, there were tons of other things.

15:16.170 --> 15:21.130
The toy I just bought at regular price
unfortunately went on sale for 50% off!

15:21.380 --> 15:24.710
When I was eating,
I unfortunately bit the inside of my mouth!

15:24.960 --> 15:29.170
Even yesterday, I mistook my face wash
for my toothpaste and brushed my teeth with that...

15:29.460 --> 15:30.670
unfortunately!

15:30.790 --> 15:32.750
Maybe that was just you not paying attention?

15:33.630 --> 15:36.580
It's no good, I can't reach it. Elda, do it for me.

15:36.960 --> 15:41.420
B-but I might unfortunately
fall off the chair and die, though.

15:41.420 --> 15:44.210
You can reach it even without
standing on the chair, Elda.

15:44.540 --> 15:45.960
And you're immortal in the first place.

15:45.960 --> 15:47.630
Y-you're right...

15:47.790 --> 15:52.580
B-but wait! Electrocution!
I might unfortunately get electrocuted!

15:53.630 --> 15:56.960
I'll do it. I'll get the stepladder.

15:58.540 --> 16:02.460
I know! While I'm out there,
I'll bring you an amulet from the shop!

16:02.880 --> 16:06.210
The power of our amulet
will kick your "unluckiness" to the curb!

16:06.460 --> 16:12.330
We can't depend on our amulet!
I mean, I'm the one being worshipped here!

16:12.500 --> 16:14.830
Have some more faith in yourself, shrine deity!

16:18.040 --> 16:22.920
I have no choice... It's come to this,
so now I'll resort to "tsujiura" for the first time in awhile!

16:23.290 --> 16:24.330
Tsujiura?

16:24.580 --> 16:26.630
It was a popular method of fortune telling
in the Edo days.

16:27.040 --> 16:28.710
A crossroad in the evening...

16:28.710 --> 16:34.130
Basically, they stand at an intersection, listening to
the conversations of passersby, and tell fortunes.

16:30.000 --> 16:31.380
<b>Tsujiura</b>

16:34.330 --> 16:36.380
<b>Onion</b>

16:34.630 --> 16:37.710
It was thought that crossroads
are places that the gods also pass through.

16:37.210 --> 16:39.210
<b>Carrot</b>

16:38.210 --> 16:41.460
We see those words as something entrusted to the gods.

16:39.210 --> 16:41.670
<b>Potato</b>

16:40.210 --> 16:41.670
<b>for dinner!</b>

16:40.210 --> 16:41.670
<b>Have curry</b>

16:42.250 --> 16:46.460
You can get an oracle about what to do
to improve your luck, according to the tsujiura.

16:46.580 --> 16:52.670
Huh? As a miko, I'm not sure I like that my shrine deity
would resort to the words of another god...

16:53.170 --> 16:57.210
Well, don't say that... I'm just an elf, after all.

16:58.540 --> 17:03.500
Even in the Edo days, when I was worried
about something I often resorted to tsujiura.

17:04.330 --> 17:05.750
I-I see...

17:06.330 --> 17:10.580
Maybe gods had a lot more responsibility
in the Edo days than they do now.

17:10.790 --> 17:14.170
Things like, how I could do a better job
skipping out on rituals...

17:14.420 --> 17:17.080
You should feel more of
a sense of responsibility as a god.

17:24.040 --> 17:27.830
Huh?! Are you waiting for someone to come here?

17:27.830 --> 17:29.750
Even if we're not at a crossroad?!

17:29.880 --> 17:35.040
I-I can't possibly go to the intersection of a city
with a ton of people walking by!

17:36.750 --> 17:38.790
Not even worshippers have come.

17:39.170 --> 17:40.580
Maybe they gave up on you?

17:41.790 --> 17:44.790
I'm home, Sis, Elda-sama!

17:44.790 --> 17:46.210
Oh, Koyuzu.

17:46.790 --> 17:50.790
Some people who came to worship
saw the two of you and left, you know?

17:50.920 --> 17:53.710
They said they would hate
to interrupt your game of hide and seek.

17:53.920 --> 17:55.380
What?! Really?!

17:55.750 --> 18:00.290
Is that why no one is coming?
I'm sorry I made them uncomfortable.

18:00.880 --> 18:02.750
What are you doing over here?

18:03.170 --> 18:05.080
Elda says she wants to improve her luck.

18:05.630 --> 18:07.880
I-I've had no luck recently.

18:08.330 --> 18:13.710
Oh, I get it. Then I'll make you something yummy
so you can feel better!

18:14.500 --> 18:15.920
What do you want for dinner?

18:19.750 --> 18:25.250
<b>What do you</b>

18:19.750 --> 18:25.250
<b>want for dinner?</b>

18:19.750 --> 18:25.250
<b>What do you</b>

18:19.750 --> 18:25.250
<b>want for dinner?</b>

18:19.830 --> 18:25.290
What do you want for dinner? What do you want for dinner...?

18:21.130 --> 18:24.290
No way... Is this the oracle?

18:25.250 --> 18:32.210
<b>What do you</b>

18:25.250 --> 18:32.210
<b>want for dinner?</b>

18:25.250 --> 18:32.210
<b>What do you</b>

18:25.250 --> 18:32.210
<b>want for dinner?</b>

18:25.750 --> 18:31.080
"What do you want for dinner?" What could possibly
be the meaning behind those words?!

18:32.290 --> 18:35.420
Uh, I think it means "What do you want for dinner?"

18:35.420 --> 18:36.710
Th-that's right!

18:36.960 --> 18:39.330
Can we have sea bream for dinner?

18:40.540 --> 18:42.580
The sea bream at this time of year
may not be very good...

18:42.580 --> 18:44.210
O-oh, okay...

18:44.580 --> 18:46.920
Why sea bream? Because it brings you luck?

18:47.170 --> 18:50.330
Yes, that and I want the bones.

18:50.830 --> 18:52.920
It's called a bream within a bream,

18:52.920 --> 18:57.330
where the bones between the gill and the pectoral fin
are shaped like the sea bream.

18:58.040 --> 19:01.540
And the fact that in the lucky sea bream,
there's another lucky sea bream,

18:59.580 --> 19:02.250
<b>Bream within a bream</b>

19:01.540 --> 19:05.420
it's been regarded as a lucky charm
ever since the Edo days.

19:05.580 --> 19:08.330
Wow! That sounds powerful!

19:08.540 --> 19:12.080
Ah! If you want mackerel, I have a good one!
One from this morning!

19:13.290 --> 19:14.880
Mackerel's not gonna work out!

19:14.880 --> 19:16.330
Mackerel is fine, though.

19:16.670 --> 19:19.710
It's shaped a little differently,
but you can find all that in mackerel, too.

19:19.710 --> 19:24.630
For real?! But then it won't be a bream within a bream,
it'll be a mackerel within a mackerel...

19:24.880 --> 19:28.460
I-in any case, I'll remove the bones and slice it!

19:29.420 --> 19:31.040
Oooh!

19:31.630 --> 19:36.710
A bream within a bream!
You're amazing Koito, it's so well done!

19:38.540 --> 19:40.210
But it's a mackerel within a mackerel, isn't it?

19:40.380 --> 19:41.750
S-Sis...

19:43.210 --> 19:49.880
I kind of feel like my luck has improved a bit!
This is the power of the bream within a bream!

19:50.500 --> 19:53.460
It feels like everything will go well from now on!

19:53.670 --> 19:58.210
Then, Elda, do you wanna put your luck to the test?
We'll try it out on my fortune slips!

19:58.210 --> 20:01.790
Oh, that sounds good! Just the thing I need!

20:05.130 --> 20:09.380
Okay. If Grampa finds us he'll get angry,
so we're doing this on the low.

20:09.380 --> 20:10.170
Yeah.

20:10.460 --> 20:13.920
O-okay, I'm gonna pull the luckiest slip!

20:14.330 --> 20:17.670
Come to me, excellent luck! Come to me, excellent luck!

20:19.920 --> 20:21.960
I-it's this one!

20:22.210 --> 20:23.420
<b>FORTUNE</b>

20:23.580 --> 20:25.630
<b>BAD LUCK</b>

20:23.580 --> 20:25.630
<b>A LITTLE</b>

20:23.590 --> 20:25.630
<b>ROUGH</b>

20:26.460 --> 20:29.210
Not even the power of
the bream within a bream can help me.

20:29.420 --> 20:31.250
That's what you get from a mackerel within a mackerel.

20:31.330 --> 20:36.170
Elda-sama! Don't give up!
Hold on to this and try pulling one more!

20:36.540 --> 20:40.250
Th-this is... A four-leaf clover!

20:40.330 --> 20:42.290
It's my good luck charm!

20:42.670 --> 20:44.540
Th-thanks, Koyuzu!

20:44.670 --> 20:46.540
Now that I have this, perhaps...

20:46.790 --> 20:49.000
<b>SLIGHTLY GOOD LUCK</b>

20:46.790 --> 20:49.000
<b>ADVANCE</b>

20:46.790 --> 20:49.000
<b>SLOWLY</b>

20:47.670 --> 20:48.960
I got a little boost!

20:49.380 --> 20:52.000
Elda! You can borrow some of my luck, too!

20:52.540 --> 20:55.210
Th-this is.... a mechanical pencil!

20:56.500 --> 20:57.330
Why?

20:57.750 --> 21:00.880
When I use it on a test, I get a good grade sometimes!

21:01.130 --> 21:02.460
I-I see.

21:03.080 --> 21:05.380
O-okay, this time for sure...

21:05.380 --> 21:08.080
It's going to work! Come to me!

21:08.420 --> 21:10.210
<b>EXCELLENT LUCK</b>

21:08.420 --> 21:10.210
<b>IT MAY DO</b>

21:08.420 --> 21:10.210
<b>SOME GOOD!</b>

21:10.330 --> 21:15.420
Hooray! I got "Excellent Luck"! Sayonara, unluckiness!
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!<b></b>

21:16.040 --> 21:18.630
That's super amazing, you really got it!

21:18.750 --> 21:20.210
You did it, Elda-sama!

21:20.540 --> 21:25.500
Thanks, I pulled "Excellent Luck"
with all of our powers combined!

21:26.880 --> 21:29.290
Ah... Grampa...

21:31.380 --> 21:33.380
K-Kikujirou...

21:36.630 --> 21:42.630
The elf, the miko, and the little sister
all together got happily yelled at.

21:43.920 --> 21:49.170
I-Is this unlucky? Or just anger?

21:49.170 --> 21:49.830
Shh!

23:23.630 --> 23:26.460
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

23:25.000 --> 23:27.960
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

23:27.290 --> 23:32.710
Spanning more than 400 years since the Edo Period,
is Takamimi Shrine.

23:27.960 --> 23:31.420
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

23:47.500 --> 23:52.580
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

23:53.460 --> 23:56.000
was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

23:57.210 --> 24:01.580
Hooray... I got a limited edition Frog Panzer...
